(function(E){ const x = E["exam-03"] = E["exam-03"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x03-l4"] = {"id":"x03-l4","patterns":["L4-nature","PARA-signpost"],"title":{"en":"Listening Part 4: a nature lecture","tr":"Listening Part 4: bir doğa dersi","fa":"Listening Part 4: سخنرانی‌ای درباره‌ی طبیعت"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to complete ten notes during a lecture about plants and rivers: follow the headings with the lecturer’s signposts, catch the point that follows \"but\", and write one word in the form you hear.","tr":"Bu derste bitkiler ve nehirler hakkındaki bir ders sırasında on notu tamamlamayı öğreneceksin: başlıkları öğretim üyesinin yön gösteren ifadeleriyle takip edecek, \"but\"tan sonra gelen noktayı yakalayacak ve tek kelimeyi duyduğun biçimde yazacaksın.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری در طول یک سخنرانی درباره‌ی گیاه و رودخانه ده یادداشت را کامل کنی: عنوان‌ها را با جمله‌های راهنمای استاد دنبال کنی، نکته‌ای را که بعد از «but» می‌آید بگیری و یک کلمه را به همان شکلی که می‌شنوی بنویسی."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Listening Part 4: a nature lecture","tr":"Listening Part 4: bir doğa dersi","fa":"Listening Part 4: سخنرانی‌ای درباره‌ی طبیعت"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to complete ten notes during a lecture about plants and rivers: follow the headings with the lecturer’s signposts, catch the point that follows \"but\", and write one word in the form you hear.","tr":"Bu derste bitkiler ve nehirler hakkındaki bir ders sırasında on notu tamamlamayı öğreneceksin: başlıkları öğretim üyesinin yön gösteren ifadeleriyle takip edecek, \"but\"tan sonra gelen noktayı yakalayacak ve tek kelimeyi duyduğun biçimde yazacaksın.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری در طول یک سخنرانی درباره‌ی گیاه و رودخانه ده یادداشت را کامل کنی: عنوان‌ها را با جمله‌های راهنمای استاد دنبال کنی، نکته‌ای را که بعد از «but» می‌آید بگیری و یک کلمه را به همان شکلی که می‌شنوی بنویسی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"10"},{"label":{"en":"Speakers","tr":"Konuşan","fa":"گوینده"},"value":"1"},{"label":{"en":"Word limit","tr":"Kelime sınırı","fa":"سقف کلمه"},"value":{"en":"1 word","tr":"1 kelime","fa":"۱ کلمه"}}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: invasive plants on riverbanks","tr":"Bu sınav: nehir kıyılarında istilacı bitkiler","fa":"این آزمون: گیاهان مهاجم در کناره‌ی رودخانه"},"intro":{"en":"Part 4 is one academic lecture. Animals, plants and ecosystems are among its most frequent subjects. The talk usually moves from causes to examples to solutions, and the notes follow the same order.","tr":"Part 4 tek bir akademik derstir. Hayvanlar, bitkiler ve ekosistemler en sık konularındandır. Konuşma genelde nedenlerden örneklere, oradan çözümlere ilerler; notlar da aynı sırayı izler.","fa":"Part 4 یک سخنرانی دانشگاهی است. حیوان، گیاه و بوم‌سازگان از پرتکرارترین موضوع‌هایش هستند. صحبت معمولاً از علت‌ها به مثال‌ها و بعد به راه‌حل‌ها می‌رود و یادداشت‌ها هم همین ترتیب را دارند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x03-l4-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["L4-nature","PARA-signpost"],"often":{"pattern":"L4-nature","n":14,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 14 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 14’ünde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۴ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"A lecture on invasive plants","tr":"İstilacı bitkiler üzerine bir ders","fa":"سخنرانی‌ای درباره‌ی گیاهان مهاجم"},"asks":{"en":"A lecturer explains why riverbanks are easily invaded by plants from other countries, describes two examples and the damage they do, then explains how they are controlled and what the future holds.","tr":"Bir öğretim üyesi nehir kıyılarının neden başka ülkelerden gelen bitkilerce kolayca istila edildiğini açıklıyor, iki örneği ve verdikleri zararı anlatıyor, sonra bunların nasıl kontrol edildiğini ve geleceği anlatıyor.","fa":"یک استاد توضیح می‌دهد چرا کناره‌ی رودخانه‌ها راحت مورد هجوم گیاهانِ آمده از کشورهای دیگر قرار می‌گیرند، دو نمونه و آسیبشان را شرح می‌دهد و بعد می‌گوید چطور کنترلشان می‌کنند و آینده چه می‌شود."},"fields":["Why rivers are vulnerable","Example 1","Example 2","Control","The future"],"words":[{"a":"invasive","b":"spreading and causing harm","tr":"istilacı","fa":"مهاجم"},{"a":"native","b":"that has always grown here","tr":"yerli","fa":"بومی"},{"a":"vulnerable","b":"easily harmed","tr":"savunmasız, hassas","fa":"آسیب‌پذیر"},{"a":"downstream","b":"in the direction the river flows","tr":"akıntı yönünde","fa":"پایین‌دست رودخانه"},{"a":"disturbance","b":"damage that clears the ground","tr":"bozulma, tahribat","fa":"آشفتگی، به‌هم‌ریختگی"},{"a":"ornamental","b":"grown for its beauty","tr":"süs bitkisi","fa":"زینتی"},{"a":"ripe","b":"fully developed / ready","tr":"olgun","fa":"رسیده"},{"a":"an annual","b":"a plant that lives for one year","tr":"tek yıllık bitki","fa":"گیاه یک‌ساله"},{"a":"crowd out","b":"take the space of other plants","tr":"diğerlerini bastırmak","fa":"جای بقیه را تنگ کردن"},{"a":"a natural enemy","b":"an animal or organism that attacks it","tr":"doğal düşman","fa":"دشمن طبیعی"},{"a":"established","b":"growing well and hard to remove","tr":"yerleşmiş","fa":"جاافتاده"},{"a":"early detection","b":"finding it quickly","tr":"erken tespit","fa":"شناسایی زودهنگام"}],"traps":[{"en":"\"You might think the main problem is X... But in some ways the bigger problem is Y.\" The note usually wants Y.","tr":"\"Ana sorunun X olduğunu düşünebilirsin... Ama bazı açılardan daha büyük sorun Y.\" Not genelde Y’yi ister.","fa":"«شاید فکر کنی مشکل اصلی X است... اما از بعضی جهات مشکل بزرگ‌تر Y است». یادداشت معمولاً Y را می‌خواهد."},{"en":"Nature lectures are full of plurals (seeds, roots, insects). If you hear the s, write the s.","tr":"Doğa dersleri çoğul isimlerle doludur (seeds, roots, insects). s’yi duyuyorsan s’yi yaz.","fa":"سخنرانی‌های طبیعت پر از اسم جمع‌اند (seeds، roots، insects). اگر s را می‌شنوی، s را بنویس."}],"example":{"text":"\"People blame the cold for the beetle’s decline, but in fact the main cause is the loss of old trees.\"","item":"Main cause of decline: loss of old ___","answer":"trees","why":{"en":"The cold is what people blame. \"In fact\" gives the cause; the plural is kept.","tr":"Soğuk, insanların suçladığı şey. \"In fact\" nedeni veriyor; çoğul korunuyor.","fa":"سرما چیزی است که مردم مقصرش می‌دانند. «in fact» علت را می‌دهد؛ جمع حفظ می‌شود."}}},{"id":"L4-nature","ctx":["L4-nature"],"title":{"en":"Animals, plants and ecosystems","tr":"Hayvanlar, bitkiler ve ekosistemler","fa":"حیوان‌ها، گیاهان و زیست‌بوم‌ها"},"asks":{"en":"A lecturer explains a species, a plant or an ecosystem: where it lives, what it eats, how it behaves, what threatens it and what researchers are doing. The notes follow those headings.","tr":"Bir öğretim görevlisi bir türü, bir bitkiyi ya da bir ekosistemi anlatır: nerede yaşadığı, ne yediği, nasıl davrandığı, onu neyin tehdit ettiği ve araştırmacıların ne yaptığı. Notlar bu başlıkları izler.","fa":"یک سخنران یک گونه، یک گیاه یا یک زیست‌بوم را توضیح می‌دهد: کجا زندگی می‌کند، چه می‌خورد، چه رفتاری دارد، چه چیزی تهدیدش می‌کند و پژوهشگرها چه می‌کنند. یادداشت‌ها همین عنوان‌ها را دنبال می‌کنند."},"fields":["Habitat","Diet","Behaviour","Threats","Research methods","Conservation","Uses to humans"],"words":[{"a":"habitat","b":"where it lives / its natural home","tr":"yaşam alanı","fa":"زیستگاه"},{"a":"predators","b":"animals that hunt it","tr":"avcı hayvanlar","fa":"شکارچی‌ها"},{"a":"prey","b":"the animals it hunts","tr":"av","fa":"طعمه"},{"a":"species","b":"a type of animal or plant","tr":"tür","fa":"گونه"},{"a":"breed","b":"produce young / have babies","tr":"üremek","fa":"تولیدمثل کردن"},{"a":"migrate","b":"travel long distances every year","tr":"göç etmek","fa":"مهاجرت کردن"},{"a":"decline","b":"fall in numbers","tr":"azalma","fa":"کاهش"},{"a":"threat","b":"a danger to its survival","tr":"tehdit","fa":"تهدید"},{"a":"native","b":"it has always lived here","tr":"yerli","fa":"بومی"},{"a":"invasive","b":"brought in from elsewhere and spreading","tr":"istilacı","fa":"مهاجم"},{"a":"soil","b":"the ground plants grow in","tr":"toprak","fa":"خاک"},{"a":"track","b":"follow where it goes with a small device","tr":"izlemek","fa":"ردیابی کردن"},{"a":"conservation","b":"protecting it","tr":"koruma","fa":"حفاظت"}],"traps":[{"en":"Plurals and spelling count: insects, seeds, leaves. Write the form you hear.","tr":"Çoğul ve yazım önemlidir: insects, seeds, leaves. Duyduğun biçimi yaz.","fa":"جمع و املا مهم است: insects، seeds، leaves. همان شکلی را که می‌شنوی بنویس."},{"en":"An old belief comes first: \"it was once thought to eat fish, but in fact it mainly eats...\". Write what comes after \"in fact\".","tr":"Önce eski bir inanış gelir: \"bir zamanlar balık yediği sanılıyordu ama aslında çoğunlukla ... yiyor\". \"In fact\"ten sonra geleni yaz.","fa":"اول یک باور قدیمی می‌آید: «زمانی فکر می‌کردند ماهی می‌خورد، ولی در واقع بیشتر ... می‌خورد». چیزی را بنویس که بعد از «in fact» می‌آید."}],"example":{"lines":[["Lecturer","For a long time, people believed these birds nested on cliffs."],["Lecturer","But recent tracking shows that most of them actually nest in old trees, well away from the coast."]],"item":"Nesting site: mainly old ___   (ONE WORD ONLY)","answer":"trees","why":{"en":"Cliffs are the old belief. \"Actually nest in old trees\": write trees, with the s.","tr":"Kayalıklar eski inanış. \"Actually nest in old trees\": trees yaz, s ile.","fa":"صخره‌ها باور قدیمی است. «Actually nest in old trees»: بنویس trees، با s."}},"general":true,"patterns":["L4-nature"],"often":{"pattern":"L4-nature","n":14,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 14 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 14’ünde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۴ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Ten notes, no break","tr":"On not, ara yok","fa":"ده یادداشت، بدون مکث"},"body":{"en":"Questions 31-40 are notes under headings. You have about 45 seconds to read them, and then the lecture plays once without a break. Write ONE WORD ONLY in each gap.","tr":"Soru 31-40 başlıklar altındaki notlardır. Okumak için yaklaşık 45 saniyen var, sonra ders arasız bir kez çalınır. Her boşluğa ONE WORD ONLY yaz.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۳۱ تا ۴۰ یادداشت‌هایی زیر عنوان‌ها هستند. حدود ۴۵ ثانیه برای خواندنشان وقت داری و بعد سخنرانی یک بار و بدون مکث پخش می‌شود. در هر جای خالی ONE WORD ONLY بنویس."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Predict, then follow","tr":"Tahmin et, sonra takip et","fa":"حدس بزن، بعد دنبال کن"},"steps":[{"en":"In the reading time, decide what each gap needs: a thing, an action, a result, a group of people.","tr":"Okuma süresinde her boşluğun neye ihtiyacı olduğuna karar ver: bir şey, bir eylem, bir sonuç, bir grup insan.","fa":"در زمان خواندن تصمیم بگیر هر جای خالی چه می‌خواهد: یک چیز، یک کار، یک نتیجه، گروهی از آدم‌ها."},{"en":"Move to the next heading when you hear \"Let’s turn to\", \"Now, what can be done?\" or \"Finally\".","tr":"\"Let’s turn to\", \"Now, what can be done?\" ya da \"Finally\" duyduğunda bir sonraki başlığa geç.","fa":"وقتی «Let’s turn to»، «Now, what can be done?» یا «Finally» را شنیدی برو سراغ عنوان بعدی."},{"en":"After \"but\", \"in fact\" or \"the bigger problem\", expect the answer.","tr":"\"But\", \"in fact\" ya da \"the bigger problem\"dan sonra cevabı bekle.","fa":"بعد از «but»، «in fact» یا «the bigger problem» منتظر جواب باش."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"Printed words and plurals","tr":"Yazılı kelimeler ve çoğullar","fa":"کلمه‌های چاپ‌شده و جمع‌ها"},"body":{"en":"If the note already says \"serious\" or \"native\", do not write it again: one word only. And keep the form you hear. \"Volunteers\" and \"volunteer\" are different answers.","tr":"Notta zaten \"serious\" ya da \"native\" yazıyorsa onu tekrar yazma: yalnızca bir kelime. Duyduğun biçimi koru. \"Volunteers\" ile \"volunteer\" farklı cevaplardır.","fa":"اگر یادداشت از قبل «serious» یا «native» را دارد، دوباره ننویسش: فقط یک کلمه. و شکلی را که می‌شنوی نگه دار. «volunteers» و «volunteer» دو جواب متفاوت‌اند."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One note, step by step","tr":"Bir not, adım adım","fa":"یک یادداشت، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Complete the notes below. Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer.","item":"Wetland birds · nests are often destroyed by ___","lines":[["Lecturer","You might expect foxes to be the main danger. In fact, most nests are lost to rising water during storms."]],"answer":"storms","walk":[{"en":"The gap follows \"destroyed by\", so it needs a noun: a cause.","tr":"Boşluk \"destroyed by\"dan sonra geliyor; bir isim, yani bir neden gerekiyor.","fa":"جای خالی بعد از «destroyed by» است، پس یک اسم لازم است: یک علت."},{"en":"Foxes are \"what you might expect\", then \"In fact\" changes the point.","tr":"Tilkiler \"beklediğin\" şey; sonra \"In fact\" noktayı değiştiriyor.","fa":"روباه‌ها «چیزی است که انتظارش را داری» و بعد «In fact» حرف را عوض می‌کند."},{"en":"Rising water \"during storms\": write storms, plural.","tr":"\"Fırtınalar sırasında\" yükselen su: storms yaz, çoğul.","fa":"آبی که «در طوفان‌ها» بالا می‌آید: storms را بنویس، جمع."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Note: \"the birds build their nests in old ___\" (ONE WORD ONLY). You hear: \"They build their nests in old walls, never in trees.\" What do you write?","options":["trees","walls","old walls"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"\"old\" is printed, so write one word: walls, plural as you hear it. Trees are ruled out by \"never\".","tr":"\"old\" yazılı; tek kelime yaz: walls, duyduğun gibi çoğul. Ağaçlar \"never\" ile eleniyor.","fa":"«old» چاپ شده، پس یک کلمه بنویس: walls، جمع همان‌طور که می‌شنوی. درخت‌ها با «never» رد می‌شوند."}},"remember":{"en":"Follow the headings, expect the answer after \"but\" or \"in fact\", and write one word in the form you hear.","tr":"Başlıkları takip et, cevabı \"but\" ya da \"in fact\"ten sonra bekle ve tek kelimeyi duyduğun biçimde yaz.","fa":"عنوان‌ها را دنبال کن، جواب را بعد از «but» یا «in fact» انتظار داشته باش و یک کلمه را به همان شکلی که می‌شنوی بنویس."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x03-l4-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-03","unit":"x03-l4"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"listening","part":"Listening Part 4","title":{"en":"Invasive plants on riverbanks","tr":"Nehir kıyılarında istilacı bitkiler","fa":"گیاهان مهاجم در کناره‌ی رودخانه"},"timed":8,"ctx":["L4-nature"],"script":[{"who":"Lecturer","line":"Good morning. In today's lecture on freshwater ecology, I'm going to look at invasive plants, that is, plants brought from other parts of the world that spread so successfully that they harm the native ecosystem. I'll concentrate on riverbanks, because rivers are where some of the worst problems in Britain are found."},{"who":"Lecturer","line":"So, first of all, why are rivers so vulnerable? There are two main reasons. The first is that a river is a very efficient transport system. Any plant that grows on a bank can drop its seeds into the water, and the current will carry those seeds downstream, sometimes for many kilometres, before leaving them on a new stretch of bank. The second reason is disturbance. Riverbanks are regularly disturbed by floods, which strip away existing plants and leave fresh, bare mud. For a fast-growing newcomer, that bare ground is an open invitation."},{"who":"Lecturer","line":"Let's turn to our first example, Himalayan balsam. It's a tall plant, often two metres or more, with attractive pink flowers, and that attractiveness is exactly why it's here. It was brought to Britain in the first half of the nineteenth century as a garden plant, and gardeners loved it. Unfortunately, it didn't stay in the gardens for long."},{"who":"Lecturer","line":"The secret of its success is the way it spreads its seeds. When the seed pods are ripe, they explode at the slightest touch, throwing the seeds several metres. A single plant can produce hundreds of seeds, and many of them land in the water and are carried away. By the twentieth century, balsam had spread along river systems across most of the country."},{"who":"Lecturer","line":"Why does this matter? You might think the main problem is simply that balsam crowds out other plants, and it certainly does that. But in some ways the bigger problem comes in winter. Balsam is an annual, so it dies back completely in the autumn. Where it has replaced the native plants, whose roots used to hold the soil together all year, the banks are left bare, and the result is erosion. Soil is washed into the river, which damages the gravel beds where fish lay their eggs."},{"who":"Lecturer","line":"There's a less obvious effect too. Balsam produces a lot of sugary nectar, more than most of our native flowers. So it attracts bees away from native flowers, which then produce fewer seeds. In other words, the damage isn't only to the plants it replaces directly."},{"who":"Lecturer","line":"Our second example is giant hogweed, which, as the name suggests, is enormous: it can reach four or five metres in height. Like balsam, it was introduced as an ornamental plant, and like balsam, its seeds travel along rivers. But hogweed is a problem for people as well as for wildlife. Its sap contains chemicals that react with sunlight, and if it gets on your skin and the skin is then exposed to the sun, it can cause serious burns. Every summer, children who play near rivers are injured in this way, so warning signs are now common along affected stretches of river."},{"who":"Lecturer","line":"Now, what can be done? For balsam, the most effective method is surprisingly simple: the plants are pulled up by hand before the seeds ripen. Its roots are shallow, so this is easy work, and it's mostly done by volunteers, in organised groups that work their way down a river from the top. Starting at the top is important, of course, because otherwise seeds from further up will simply replace the plants you've removed."},{"who":"Lecturer","line":"Pulling by hand can't cover every river, though, so scientists have also looked for a natural enemy. In its native region in the Himalayas, balsam is attacked by a rust, a kind of fungus that damages its leaves. After years of testing to make sure it wouldn't harm any other plant, this fungus has been released at a number of sites in Britain. The early results are promising, but it's too soon to say how well it will work over large areas."},{"who":"Lecturer","line":"Hogweed, by contrast, can't safely be pulled up by volunteers because of the sap, so it's usually treated with chemicals by trained teams wearing protective clothing. And because its seeds can survive in the soil for several years, a site has to be checked again and again."},{"who":"Lecturer","line":"Finally, the future. Most experts agree that we'll never remove these plants completely. The aim now is to stop new invaders before they become established, and for that, early detection is everything. Here the public has a real role to play. Several phone apps now let walkers photograph a plant and send the location to scientists, and these reports from the public have already helped to find new outbreaks while they were still small enough to deal with. So if you're walking by a river this summer, keep your eyes open."}],"notes":{"title":"Invasive plants on riverbanks","headings":["Why rivers are vulnerable","Himalayan balsam","Giant hogweed","Control","The future"],"extra":["Giant hogweed · can grow to four or five metres","Control · hogweed is treated with chemicals by trained teams"]},"groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 31-40. Complete the notes below. Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer.","qtype":"note","questions":[{"n":31,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Why rivers are vulnerable · the current carries plants’ ___ downstream to new banks","accept":["seeds"],"limit":1,"evidence":"will carry those seeds downstream","why":{"en":"\"The current will carry those seeds downstream.\" Plural.","tr":"\"Akıntı o tohumları akış yönünde taşır.\" Çoğul.","fa":"«جریان آب آن دانه‌ها را به پایین‌دست می‌برد». جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":32,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Why rivers are vulnerable · banks are often stripped bare by ___","accept":["floods"],"limit":1,"evidence":"Riverbanks are regularly disturbed by floods","why":{"en":"\"Regularly disturbed by floods, which strip away existing plants\".","tr":"\"Mevcut bitkileri söküp götüren sellerle düzenli olarak bozulur\".","fa":"«مرتب با سیل‌هایی که گیاهان موجود را می‌کنند به هم می‌ریزند»."},"trap":["TR-plural","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":33,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Himalayan balsam · first brought to Britain as a ___ plant","accept":["garden"],"limit":1,"evidence":"as a garden plant","why":{"en":"\"Brought to Britain... as a garden plant, and gardeners loved it.\"","tr":"\"İngiltere’ye... bir bahçe bitkisi olarak getirildi ve bahçıvanlar onu çok sevdi.\"","fa":"«به‌عنوان گیاه باغچه به بریتانیا آورده شد و باغبان‌ها عاشقش شدند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":34,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Himalayan balsam · ripe seed pods ___ when touched, throwing the seeds several metres","accept":["explode"],"limit":1,"evidence":"they explode at the slightest touch","why":{"en":"\"They explode at the slightest touch.\"","tr":"\"En ufak dokunuşta patlarlar.\"","fa":"«با کوچک‌ترین تماس می‌ترکند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":35,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Himalayan balsam · when it dies in winter, bare banks suffer from ___","accept":["erosion"],"limit":1,"evidence":"the result is erosion","why":{"en":"Crowding out other plants is not the bigger problem. In winter \"the banks are left bare, and the result is erosion\".","tr":"Diğer bitkileri bastırması daha büyük sorun değil. Kışın \"kıyılar çıplak kalır ve sonuç erozyondur\".","fa":"جا تنگ کردن برای گیاهان دیگر مشکل بزرگ‌تر نیست. در زمستان «کناره‌ها لخت می‌مانند و نتیجه فرسایش است»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":36,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Himalayan balsam · its nectar draws ___ away from native flowers","accept":["bees"],"limit":1,"evidence":"it attracts bees away from native flowers","why":{"en":"\"It attracts bees away from native flowers\": draws = attracts.","tr":"\"Arıları yerli çiçeklerden uzaklaştırıp kendine çeker\": draws = attracts.","fa":"«زنبورها را از گل‌های بومی به سمت خودش می‌کشد»: draws یعنی attracts."},"trap":["TR-plural","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":37,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Giant hogweed · sap on the skin, followed by sunlight, can cause serious ___","accept":["burns"],"limit":1,"evidence":"it can cause serious burns","why":{"en":"\"It can cause serious burns.\" \"serious\" is printed: write one word.","tr":"\"Ciddi yanıklara yol açabilir.\" \"serious\" yazılı: tek kelime yaz.","fa":"«می‌تواند سوختگی‌های جدی ایجاد کند». «serious» چاپ شده: یک کلمه بنویس."},"trap":["TR-limit","TR-plural"]},{"n":38,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Control · balsam is pulled up by hand, mostly by ___","accept":["volunteers"],"limit":1,"evidence":"it's mostly done by volunteers","why":{"en":"\"It’s mostly done by volunteers, in organised groups.\" Plural.","tr":"\"Çoğunlukla gönüllüler tarafından, düzenli gruplar hâlinde yapılır.\" Çoğul.","fa":"«بیشتر توسط داوطلب‌ها، در گروه‌های سازمان‌یافته، انجام می‌شود». جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":39,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Control · a ___ from the Himalayas has been released to attack balsam","accept":["fungus","rust"],"limit":1,"evidence":"a kind of fungus that damages its leaves","why":{"en":"\"A rust, a kind of fungus that damages its leaves.\" Both words name the same thing, so fungus or rust is accepted; one word only.","tr":"\"Bir pas, yapraklarına zarar veren bir tür mantar.\" İki kelime de aynı şeyi adlandırıyor; fungus da rust da kabul edilir; yalnızca tek kelime.","fa":"«یک زنگ (rust)، نوعی قارچ که به برگ‌هایش آسیب می‌زند». هر دو کلمه همان چیز را نام می‌برند، پس fungus یا rust هر دو قبول است؛ فقط یک کلمه."},"trap":["TR-limit"]},{"n":40,"kind":"gap","prompt":"The future · finding new outbreaks early depends on ___ sent in by the public","accept":["reports"],"limit":1,"evidence":"these reports from the public","why":{"en":"\"These reports from the public have already helped to find new outbreaks.\" Plural.","tr":"\"Halktan gelen bu bildirimler yeni salgınları bulmaya şimdiden yardım etti.\" Çoğul.","fa":"«این گزارش‌های مردم تا حالا به پیدا کردن کانون‌های تازه کمک کرده‌اند». جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural","TR-paraphrase"]}]}],"audio":{"voices":{"Announcer":{"accent":"British (standard Southern)","gender":"M","tts":{"engine":"kokoro","voice":"bm_george"},"role":"Recorded rubric"},"Lecturer":{"accent":"British (standard Southern)","gender":"F","tts":{"engine":"kokoro","voice":"bf_isabella"},"role":"Lecturer"}},"sequence":[{"type":"announcer","text":"Part 4. You will hear a lecture about invasive plants on riverbanks. First, you have some time to look at Questions 31 to 40."},{"type":"pause","seconds":45,"note":"reading time, Questions 31-40"},{"type":"announcer","text":"Now listen carefully and answer Questions 31 to 40."},{"type":"sfx","note":"lecture-hall acoustics: slight reverb; 1.5 s between paragraphs"},{"type":"lines","from":0,"to":10},{"type":"announcer","text":"That is the end of Part 4. You now have two minutes to check your answers.","after":120}]},"id":"c-x03-l4-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-03","unit":"x03-l4"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"A \"native\" plant is one that...","options":["has always grown in that area","was brought from another country","grows only in gardens"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Native = naturally belonging to a place. The opposite here is \"invasive\" or \"introduced\".","tr":"Native = bir yere doğal olarak ait olan. Burada karşıtı \"invasive\" ya da \"introduced\".","fa":"native یعنی متعلق به همان جا به‌طور طبیعی. این‌جا متضادش «invasive» یا «introduced» است."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"Which phrase means \"in the direction the river flows\"?","options":["upstream","across the river","downstream"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Downstream = with the current. Upstream = against it.","tr":"Downstream = akıntıyla aynı yönde. Upstream = akıntıya karşı.","fa":"downstream یعنی هم‌جهت با جریان. upstream یعنی خلاف جریان."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"The lecturer says \"Now, what can be done?\" Which heading should you move to?","options":["the heading about causes","the heading about control","the first heading"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"\"What can be done?\" signals solutions: the control heading.","tr":"\"Ne yapılabilir?\" çözümlere geçildiğini gösterir: kontrol başlığı.","fa":"«چه کاری می‌شود کرد؟» نشانه‌ی رفتن سراغ راه‌حل‌هاست: عنوانِ کنترل."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Note: \"the main danger to young fish: ___\" (ONE WORD ONLY). You hear: \"You might think it’s pollution, but in fact it’s heat.\" What do you write?","options":["heat","pollution","pollution and heat"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"\"You might think\" introduces the wrong idea; \"in fact\" gives the answer.","tr":"\"Düşünebilirsin\" yanlış fikri getirir; \"in fact\" cevabı verir.","fa":"«شاید فکر کنی» ایده‌ی غلط را می‌آورد؛ «in fact» جواب را می‌دهد."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Note: \"work is done by local ___\". You hear: \"It’s mostly done by local schoolchildren.\" What do you write?","options":["schoolchild","local schoolchildren","schoolchildren"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"\"local\" is printed; write the plural you hear: schoolchildren.","tr":"\"local\" yazılı; duyduğun çoğulu yaz: schoolchildren.","fa":"«local» چاپ شده؛ جمعی را که می‌شنوی بنویس: schoolchildren."}}],"id":"c-x03-l4-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-03","unit":"x03-l4"}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
